正解
Enable just-in-time (JIT) VM access for the virtual machines in Microsoft Defender for Cloud, and configure a rule for port 3389 that requires approval and specifies a maximum request duration.
説明
This answer is correct. Just-in-time VM access in Microsoft Defender for Cloud automatically creates a "deny" rule in the network security group for the specified port and only opens temporary, time-limited access after a request is approved, closing the port again once the time expires. This directly meets the requirement for default-blocked access with limited-time, approval-based exceptions and minimal ongoing effort, since Defender for Cloud manages the rule changes automatically.
