Contoso Ltd. stores immutable audit logs in an Azure Storage account named auditlogsa. The security compliance team requires that no one—including subscription Owners—can accidentally delete this storage account, but they must still be able to write new audit log entries to it continuously without interruption. You need to configure a governance control that meets both requirements with minimal administrative overhead. What should you do?
Apply a ReadOnly lock to the auditlogsa storage account
説明
This answer is incorrect. A ReadOnly lock prevents both deletion and modification of the resource, including any write operations such as updates to properties, keys, or configuration. This would block the continuous writing of new audit log entries, failing the requirement to keep the storage account writable.
Remove the Owner role assignment from all users on the resource group containing auditlogsa
説明
This answer is incorrect. Removing Owner role assignments does not guarantee protection against deletion, since other roles (such as Contributor) or future role assignments could still permit deletion. This approach also disrupts normal administrative access and does not directly address the stated goal in a reliable, scoped way.
Create an Azure Policy definition with a deny effect that blocks delete operations on the storage account
説明
This answer is incorrect. Azure Policy is designed to evaluate and enforce resource properties and configurations at creation or update time (using effects like Deny, Audit, or Append); it is not the mechanism used to block delete actions on existing resources. Resource locks, not policy definitions, are the purpose-built governance feature for preventing deletion.
回答は正解です
Apply a CanNotDelete lock to the auditlogsa storage account
説明
This answer is correct. A CanNotDelete lock allows authorized users to read and modify (write to) the resource but blocks all delete operations, regardless of the RBAC permissions the user holds, including Owner. This satisfies both requirements: deletion is prevented while write operations for audit logging continue uninterrupted.
全体的な説明
Resource locks in Azure provide two levels of protection: ReadOnly (blocks both writes and deletes) and CanNotDelete (blocks only deletes while allowing writes). Since the scenario requires preventing deletion while still allowing continuous writes, a CanNotDelete lock is the correct governance control, and it overrides RBAC permissions for all users, including Owners.
