Locking an origin to a specific Front Door profile takes two coordinated controls. The AzureFrontDoor.Backend service tag restricts inbound traffic to the address ranges Front Door uses, but those ranges are shared by every Azure customer, so on its own the tag would still allow a stranger's profile to call the origin. Front Door stamps each request with an X-Azure-FDID header containing the profile's unique identifier, and App Service access restrictions can match on that header value. Combining the service tag with the header match means requests are accepted only when they come from Front Door infrastructure and carry Contoso's own profile ID. Private Link origins are a stronger alternative on supported tiers, but they change the publishing topology rather than simply filtering the existing one.
