Contoso Ltd. is onboarding 200 new remote employees. On their first day, each employee must set up the Microsoft Authenticator app for passwordless sign-in using their personal smartphone. Since the employees are remote and have never signed in to Microsoft Entra ID before, they do not possess any other registered authentication method (such as a password, FIDO2 key, or existing Authenticator registration) that could be used to complete the initial sign-in and registration process. IT wants to issue each new employee a short-lived credential that expires after 24 hours and can be used only to complete initial authentication method registration.

Which authentication method should the Microsoft Entra administrator configure to meet this requirement?

Certificate-based authentication
説明
This answer is incorrect. Certificate-based authentication requires a Public Key Infrastructure (PKI) and issued digital certificates, which is a separate, more complex authentication mechanism. It is not designed as a short-lived onboarding credential for bootstrapping registration of the Microsoft Authenticator app.
Windows Hello for Business
説明
This answer is incorrect. Windows Hello for Business is a device-bound biometric or PIN-based authentication method tied to a specific Windows device and requires device registration and enrollment. It does not address the scenario of remote employees using personal smartphones to register the Authenticator app without an existing credential.
FIDO2 security key
説明
This answer is incorrect. A FIDO2 security key is itself a passwordless authentication method that requires the user to already possess and register the physical hardware key; it is not a bootstrap credential used to enable registration of other methods remotely. Provisioning physical keys to 200 remote employees on day one is also impractical compared to a temporary passcode.
回答は正解です
Temporary Access Pass (TAP)
説明
This answer is correct. A Temporary Access Pass (TAP) is a time-limited passcode issued by an administrator that allows a user to sign in and register other authentication methods, including passwordless methods like Microsoft Authenticator, without needing an existing credential. TAP can be configured with a limited lifetime (such as 24 hours) and is specifically designed for onboarding scenarios like this one.
全体的な説明
The Temporary Access Pass is the Microsoft Entra ID feature purpose-built to solve the "chicken-and-egg" problem of enabling passwordless or MFA registration for users who have no existing authentication method. Administrators can configure TAP lifetime, usage limits, and one-time or reusable settings, making it ideal for time-bound onboarding scenarios like this one.
